ocg: PrintState/ViewState ON is visible even when the OCG is in /OFF (issue #6101)

pdf_is_ocg_hidden already hid a layer when its Usage event (PrintState,
ViewState, ExportState) was OFF. Any other value, including ON, fell through
to the optional-content config ON/OFF list.

Print-only OCGs (PrintState ON, ViewState OFF) are listed in /OFF so they do
not show on screen. Printing still has to draw them: Acrobat does. Without
honouring ON, Sumatra skipped the print-only fill that ocgx2 uses to clip
hyperlink text, so the link vanished on print.

Fixes https://github.com/sumatrapdfreader/sumatrapdf/issues/6101
---
diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-layer.c b/source/pdf/pdf-layer.c
index 73f118a78..fb1b1b0b1 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-layer.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-layer.c
@@ -767,6 +767,9 @@ pdf_is_ocg_hidden_imp(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, pdf_resource_stack *rd
 		es = pdf_dict_gets(ctx, obj2, event_state);
 		if (pdf_name_eq(ctx, es, PDF_NAME(OFF)))
 			return 1;
+		/* Usage event ON: visible even if the OCG is in the config OFF list. */
+		if (pdf_name_eq(ctx, es, PDF_NAME(ON)))
+			return 0;
 		return default_value;
 	}
 	else if (pdf_name_eq(ctx, type, PDF_NAME(OCMD)))
